From b7e51b5933e92734d3853bf398be0941db524332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): add PDL chain to gather_columns_kernel before
 compressor

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.

Rationale:
gather_columns_into runs immediately between the rank-major all-gather and
gather_partial_state_kernel / compress_kernel inside DeepseekCompressor._project.
Without pdl.chain() (T.pdl_sync() / T.pdl_trigger()), compress_kernel cannot
overlap its pre-wait static weight and slot-metadata preload with
gather_columns_kernel. Add pdl.chain() to gather_columns_kernel and register
gather_columns_into in tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py CHAIN,
reducing gather_columns_into -> compress_kernel chain latency across 2 GB10
boots by -19.85%..-25.52% on ratio-1 and -4.85%..-8.85% on ratio-2 across
TP3 and TP4 (M = 1..128).

Quality:
Bit-identical torch.equal output across all ranks, row counts, padding rows,
and output strides; only adds Programmatic Dependent Launch synchronization.

Tests:
131/131 gather + PDL tests and 14/14 TileLang PDL source/SASS/order audit
tests pass across 2 GPU boots on GB10 with 0 PDL violations.

Upstream status:
Local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang PDL chain completion for spark-ds41f.
